            {
                "entry_id": "ba7b2907-a06e-3f4b-86fe-48f69630a57d",
                "word": "TSPT",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2e8f487d-3e30-34ec-8bed-7843ac4e2286",
                        "entry_id": "ba7b2907-a06e-3f4b-86fe-48f69630a57d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Abréviation de trouble de stress post-traumatique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Nosologie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2985e38c-113b-4731-9ebb-fa03d470e5ce",
                                "sense_id": "2e8f487d-3e30-34ec-8bed-7843ac4e2286",
                                "text": "Le trouble de stress post-traumatique (TSPT) survient à la suite de l’expérience, directe ou indirecte, d’événements traumatiques, définis comme « l’exposition à la mort effective ou à une menace de mort, à une blessure grave ou à des violences sexuelles »."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "98883ab4-dd6c-4f97-838b-5a2200de4740",
                                "sense_id": "2e8f487d-3e30-34ec-8bed-7843ac4e2286",
                                "text": "Comme nous l’avons exprimé dans le chapitre de présentation du TSTP (chapitre 1), nous utilisons le DSM-5 comme cadre de référence dans cet ouvrage. Notons que c’est un choix qui atteint sa limite avec certaines populations puisque comme le font remarquer Korte et al. (2020), les études interculturelles montrent que les symptômes inclus dans le diagnostic du TSPT devraient éventuellement être élargis et adaptés en fonction des cultures."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "82ccfdb9-75ac-4167-99ac-5b852e0ef8c2",
                                "sense_id": "2e8f487d-3e30-34ec-8bed-7843ac4e2286",
                                "text": "À ce jour, très peu d’études françaises existent sur l’impact de la pet-therapy (ou thérapie par les animaux) auprès de patients qui souffrent d’un trouble de stress post-traumatique (TSPT)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d33c59fd-9150-4f2a-99bb-400289431b86",
                        "source_entry_id": "ba7b2907-a06e-3f4b-86fe-48f69630a57d",
                        "source_sense_id": "2e8f487d-3e30-34ec-8bed-7843ac4e2286",
                        "target_lang_word": "post-traumatic stress disorder",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "post-traumatic stress disorder",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ed6032d7-a72b-3329-8c40-842aa34adb73",
                                        "entry_id": "6ad5792a-1bb4-342c-93d3-9b7d82ab3948",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A psychological condition that develops following some stressful situation or event, with symptoms such as sleep disturbance, recurrent dreams, flashbacks, hypervigilance, depression, dissociation, withdrawal or lack of concentration."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de848901-7cd4-448c-9202-a0a78084713a",
                                                "sense_id": "ed6032d7-a72b-3329-8c40-842aa34adb73",
                                                "text": "That 200,000 public school students have been identified with symptoms of post-traumatic stress disorder since Sept. 11 should serve as a wake-up call for school-based mental health services for all students. We must not allow Sept. 11 to eclipse the post-traumatic stress disorders suffered by students from epidemics of H.I.V.-AIDS and community and domestic violence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "069417fd-9aac-44c4-9b4b-4141f5bac121",
                                                "sense_id": "ed6032d7-a72b-3329-8c40-842aa34adb73",
                                                "text": "The evidence says that enormous numbers of children who live in households in high-crime neighborhoods are experiencing the psychological equivalent of battlefield conditions.[...]Studies show that many children who live under these conditions, 30 percent or more, are developing post-traumatic stress disorder, or PTSD, similar to what we used to call “shell shock” in soldiers returning from war."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26e62468-90e7-491d-bf38-c8527b32c4be",
                                                "sense_id": "ed6032d7-a72b-3329-8c40-842aa34adb73",
                                                "text": "An example of the contract, read out in the committee said: “I understand that exposure to this content may give me post traumatic stress disorder. I will engage in a mandatory wellness coaching session but I understand that those are not conditions and may not be sufficient to prevent my contracting PTSD.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1868a38a-4144-412f-b73a-867fd8095fef",
                        "source_entry_id": "ba7b2907-a06e-3f4b-86fe-48f69630a57d",
                        "source_sense_id": "2e8f487d-3e30-34ec-8bed-7843ac4e2286",
                        "target_lang_word": "PTSD",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "PTSD",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9dc6b434-9231-32c3-8791-1a4ca8572e03",
                                        "entry_id": "298d1d00-9f97-3388-8043-f185855fa181",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Initialism of post-traumatic stress disorder."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "initialism",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e529d41-4e80-4e82-8f68-3b08e9279e32",
                                                "sense_id": "9dc6b434-9231-32c3-8791-1a4ca8572e03",
                                                "text": "I read that parents suffering from PTSD are more likely to hit their children."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab294555-697c-4643-ac24-038cfc6f328f",
                                                "sense_id": "9dc6b434-9231-32c3-8791-1a4ca8572e03",
                                                "text": "But Wisniewski explained that the most promising aromatic journeys, like those designed by Verbeek, are not always sweet smelling. Treating PTSD requires re-creating battlefield aromas, for example, while firefighters might train in smoke-scented simulations."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
